v0.3.2 CI: tarballs for linux/macos, Mach-O checks, Release on v* tags

- linux/macos artifacts now ship the bare binary plus a .tar.gz of the same file,
  so a download always yields something that runs (tar keeps the mode).
- macOS: verify the Mach-O (file/otool/exec bit), guard the ad-hoc codesign, and
  add best-effort .app/.dmg packaging (.app packed as tar).
- linux packages step pinned to --bundles deb,appimage; artifact renamed to
  OpenOCD-GUI-linux-packages.
- new release job: on v* tags, flatten the artifacts and publish them as a GitHub
  Release (softprops/action-gh-release).
- README (en/zh): how to run each artifact, why the bare Mach-O has no extension,
  quarantine/ad-hoc signing, and that artifacts come from the build run while
  Releases only appear for tags.
